From bf74df73b68c2ddceec4f4fd54048e0c2b794004 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <dev@infoverify.local>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 22:39:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix KatPay webhook silently skipping deposits that share a
 bank narration
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Root cause of the reported incident: a user's ₦10,000 transfer credited
fine, but two later ₦250 transfers into the same virtual account both
showed 'Delivered' on KatPay's dashboard while never reaching the
wallet balance.

webhook.routes.ts built its dedup key (passed to
creditDirectDepositByAccountNumber as ) by trying
 before . For a bank transfer,
 is frequently just the narration text (sender name/
account), which is IDENTICAL across every transfer the same sender
makes into the same account - wallet.service.ts's own providerRef
comment already flagged this exact risk. The ₦10,000 transfer claimed
that narration text as its providerRef; the next two ₦250 transfers
shared the same reference, so creditDirectDepositByAccountNumber's
existing-transaction dedup check (working exactly as designed) treated
them as already-processed duplicates of the first - 200 back to
KatPay, wallet untouched, and nothing in the logs distinguishes this
from a genuine redelivered webhook.

Fix: try  first (KatPay's own per-event identifier),
falling back to order_no/orderNo/reference in that order - same
fallback chain as before, just reordered. Extracted the selection into
its own exported pickKatpayTransactionReference() so it's unit-testable
without needing a live raw-body+HMAC HTTP harness for the whole route.

New test file (webhook.routes.reference.test.ts, 4 tests) locks in the
exact failure mode: three payloads sharing one  narration
but distinct uid=0(root) gid=0(root) groups=0(root)s must yield three distinct keys.

Verified: full suite now 177 passed (173 existing + 4 new), zero
regressions. tsc shows zero errors on either touched file.

Does NOT retroactively credit the two ₦250 deposits already silently
skipped in production - those need a manual wallet adjustment via
/admin/user-wallet (search the user, apply a ₦500 credit, reason:
'KatPay VA deposits sharing narration ref, not auto-credited - see
webhook.routes.ts fix').
